---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

// TEMPLATE: review this against your actual analytics, email and hosting setup
// before launch, and replace the contact email below.
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@thegoodhomelist.com';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects information about visitors, including cookies, analytics and affiliate tracking.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Privacy Policy' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric' })}</p>

      <p>
        This policy explains what information {SITE.name} collects when you visit
        {' '}<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>, how it is used, and the
        choices you have.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        Like most websites, this site collects standard technical information when you visit,
        which may include your IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating
        system, referring page, pages viewed, and the time and date of your visit. This data is
        aggregated and used to understand how the site is used and to keep it working properly.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you provide</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us, we receive whatever you choose to send, such as your name, email
        address and the contents of your message. We use it only to reply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        Cookies are small text files stored by your browser. This site and its third-party
        partners may use them to remember preferences, measure traffic, and track affiliate
        referrals so that a commission can be attributed correctly.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings. The site will still work,
        though some features may behave differently.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use privacy-conscious web analytics to measure aggregate traffic patterns, such as
        which pages are read and where visitors arrive from. We do not use analytics data to
        identify individual visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links and third parties</h2>
      <p>
        This site contains affiliate links, including links to Amazon.com. When you click one, the
        destination site may set cookies or otherwise record that you arrived from here, so that
        any resulting purchase can be credited. Those sites operate under their own privacy
        policies, which we do not control. We recommend reading them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Amazon's privacy notice is available on the Amazon website. Our own use of affiliate
        links is described in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Data sharing</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We do not share it with third parties except
        where necessary to operate the site, such as hosting and analytics providers acting on
        our behalf, or where required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        Aggregate analytics data is retained for as long as it is useful for understanding site
        performance. Messages you send us are kept only as long as needed to handle your enquiry.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on where you live, you may have the right to request access to the personal
        information we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or object to
        certain processing. Residents of the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom have
        these rights under the GDPR. Residents of California have comparable rights under the
        CCPA, including the right to know what is collected and the right to request deletion.
      </p>
      <p>
        To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from them. If you believe a child has provided us with information, contact
        us and we will delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served over HTTPS. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure,
        so we cannot guarantee absolute security, but we take reasonable measures to protect
        information.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. Changes are posted on this page with a
        revised date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can go to
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
